Data sources (see data/*/SOURCE.md for each file):
- U.S. DOT Bureau of Transportation Statistics: Reporting Carrier On-Time Performance, Form 41 Schedule B-43,
  T-100 Domestic Segment, DB1B. U.S. Government works, public domain. The viewer's traffic at the hubs comes from the
  on-time data.
- FAA Air Traffic Control System Command Center advisories (fly.faa.gov). U.S. Government works, public domain.
- FAA Aircraft Registry releasable database. U.S. Government work, public domain.
- Iowa Environmental Mesonet (Iowa State University): archived METAR, TAF, NEXRAD composites. Public domain;
  attribution to the Iowa Environmental Mesonet is appreciated and given here.
- airportsdata (MIT licence): airport coordinates and time zones.
- OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL 1.0), via Overpass: the airport twin and the 3D airport stage (runways, taxiways,
  aprons, stands, terminals, buildings), hosted with the dataset and attributed in the viewer.
- USGS The National Map, USGSImageryOnly orthoimagery: the aerial photo under the 3D stage, and the coarser imagery
  and USGSHydroCached hydrography tiles the viewer loads around it at run time. U.S. Government works, public domain.
- The viewer's US map, loaded at run time: Natural Earth shaded relief (public domain) and OpenMapTiles vector tiles
  (© OpenMapTiles, © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0), served by OpenFreeMap.

Third-party code:
- PortSimEnv v1 (FineEnvs), Apache-2.0: Three.js scene code (sky, sun, image-based light, haze, water, materials and
  instancing helpers) adapted in web/stage/*.js; each adapted file names its source on its first line.
- Three.js (MIT) and MapLibre GL JS (BSD-3-Clause), loaded by the viewer from jsDelivr, not bundled.
